<title>BELGIUM: EU confirms it cleared CEGELEC buy of AEG unit.</title>
<headline>EU confirms it cleared CEGELEC buy of AEG unit.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-09-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Commission confirmed on Friday it had cleared the acquisition by CEGELEC S.A., belonging to Alcatel Alsthom, of AEG AAT.</p>
<p>AEG AAT belongs to Germany's AEG, which is majority owned by Daimler-Benz.</p>
<p>The businesses being acquired by CEGELEC include factory automation, goods distribution systems and industrial process engineering.</p>
<p>After the deal, the two firms would have a combined market share below 15 percent in the EU as a whole or in any individual member country.</p>
<p>&quot;For these reasons, the Commission has concluded that the concentration does not create or strengthen any dominant position in the EEA (European Economic Area) or any substantial part of that area and has decided to declare it compatible with the common market and with the functioning of the EEA agreement,&quot; the Commission said in a statement. -- Brussels newsroom +32 2 287 68 11</p>
</text>
